// Test simfile with hand-worked BPM statistics, for calibrating ddr-trainer's chart analyzer
// (src/chart_analyzer.rs), whose tests check the table below. Generated by
// test_resources/make_test_simfiles.py, so edit that instead of this.
//
// A .sm file's BPMs are shared by all its charts, so each chart covers a different stretch of
// these, each BPM lasting from its beat to the next change:
//   beat    0    4    10   24   26   30   33 1/3  40   52   64
//   BPM     150  120  240  120  120  60   200     240  120  150
// The change at 26 is to the BPM it's already at, and the one at 33 1/3 is written as 33.333,
// which StepMania rounds to the nearest 48th of a beat. The statistics only cover the stretch
// from a chart's first object (a note, mine or hold end) to its last:
//   - mode is the BPM the chart spends the most seconds at (beats * 60 / BPM), adding up
//     separate stretches at the same BPM, with ties going to the smaller BPM. A chart with
//     everything on one beat takes the BPM there, and a chart with nothing in it has 0
//   - changes is how many times the BPM changes. Changes to the same BPM don't count, and
//     neither do changes before the first object, after the last, or exactly on either
//
//   chart      first beat  last beat  mode  changes
//   Beginner   -           -             0        0  nothing in it
//   Easy       10          10          240        0  one jump, on a change
//   Medium     40          58          120        1  a tie
//   Hard       5           32          120        3  seconds, not beats
//   Challenge  4           33 1/3      120        3  starts and ends on changes
//
//   Medium: 3 s at 240 (beats 40-52), then 3 s at 120 (52-58). The tie goes to 120.
//   Hard: 2.5 s at 120 (beats 5-10), 3.5 s at 240 (10-24), 3 s at 120 (24-30) and 2 s at 60
//     (30-32). 120 adds up to 5.5 s, so it's the mode, even though 240 has more beats (14 to
//     11) and the longest single stretch. It changes at 10, 24 and 30, but not at 26.
//   Challenge: 3 s at 120 (beats 4-10), 3.5 s at 240 (10-24), 3 s at 120 (24-30) and 3 1/3 s
//     at 60 (30-33 1/3). 120 adds up to 6 s. It changes at 10, 24 and 30, but not at 4 or
//     33 1/3, where its first and last notes are.
//
// The lowest and highest BPM in the same stretch, and the seconds from beat 0 to the first
// object:
//   chart      min  max  start
//   Beginner     0    0  0
//   Easy       240  240  4.6        4 beats at 150, then 6 at 120
//   Medium     120  240  16 13/30   then 14 at 240, 6 at 120, 3 1/3 at 60 and 6 2/3 at 200
//   Hard        60  240  2.1
//   Challenge   60  240  1.6
#TITLE:BPM Stats;
#ARTIST:ddr-trainer;
#MUSIC:bpm_stats.ogg;
#OFFSET:0.000000;
#BPMS:0.000=150.000,4.000=120.000,10.000=240.000,24.000=120.000,26.000=120.000,
30.000=60.000,33.333=200.000,40.000=240.000,52.000=120.000,64.000=150.000;
#STOPS:;

//---------------dance-single - nothing in it----------------
#NOTES:
     dance-single:
     nothing in it:
     Beginner:
     1:
     0.412,0.356,0.250,0.100,0.000:
// measure 0: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
,  // measure 1: empty
0000
0000
0000
0000
;

